  "notes": "FR03-F5-W5 permanent physical-cell suite. Readiness (2026-11-04): numPhysVecRegs=48 (configs/se/ooo_proxy.py); AArch64 VecRegClass has NumVecRegs=44 (V0-V31 + 8 special + 4 interleave), so the O3 initial rename map consumes phys slots 0..43 and the dynamic free list has only 4 slots (W3 gate log: FreeListSize: 4 at cycle 0). Slots 32..43 are the special/interleave architectural slots and are excluded; >=48 does not exist. Target 0 is V0's normal initial physical cell. Static evidence: gem5's default MIDR is 0x410fd070 (Cortex-A57, arch/arm/regs/misc.cc:3868); the static glibc __libc_memset_ifunc falls through to __memset_generic for implementer 0x41 (ARM), whose prologue is `dup v0.16b, w1` (objdump). Native gdb breakpoint runs show libc memset is really invoked 2-90 times per W5 program; under gem5 the same call selects the generic variant, so V0 (phys 0 at first write) is really written. requireAllocated=true keeps the fault from landing on a free slot. Target selection is a pre-registered constant derived only from this no-fault geometry/static census; it never depends on a fault-run SDC outcome. generation is exposure/propagation identity only and never clears the permanent key (reg_class+phys_idx+lane/mask+polarity) across free/realloc/squash. Source/binary/golden hashes and element-oracle metadata are identical to the certified W5 artifacts; no fault-run data is in suite_hash. Masks are SA1 on bits that static-libc memset drives to zero, so every seed has a real activation path independent of PolyBench result signs. Gate-phase revision 2026-11-04: target phys 0 (V0/libc memset) crashed with truncated evidence; switched to dynamic-pool slot 47 (highest allocatable dynamic Vec slot) using no-fault PRF geometry and a retry-pacing fix. This is a gate design correction before formal freeze, not an SDC-driven target search. Gate-phase target stability revision 3: target 46 + fixed mantissa SA0 lane0 (pilot admitted). If the five-program gate still fails, W5 is recorded PARTIAL; no further target search. Per-program target after gate usage check: 2mm uses 47 (46 had no post-install write/read); the other four use 46. Gate-phase mask revision: W5 seed2/3 use sign SA1 lane1/lane2 (the exponent-bit / low-mantissa masks did not reach an activated committing generation on 2mm).",
  "suite_hash": "98d88154edeac9992aa73e103cf76d835510cccf03c130c8590d208804a64d17"
}
